<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osman I</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osman I was the founder of the Ottoman dynasty, a Turkoman chieftain of the Kayı clan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oghuz-turks">Oghuz Turks</a>, active around 1300. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bithynia">Bithynia</a> lay on the frontier with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> and attracted ghazi warriors. His victory over a Byzantine force at Bapheus in 1301 established the military credibility on which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> was built.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osman-i.jpg" alt="Osman I" width="263" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ottoman miniature painting · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:I_Osman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
